      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Furthermore, I might add that... in the \"Community Guidelines\", it says, and I quote: \"Group moderators can employ verbal or text-based warnings, system-level warnings, kicks, or even bans to enforce their rules\".\n\nSo you advise moderating own group \"to enforce their rules\".. but it's possible in a group to ban a user who isn't even in the group?\n\nHow could a user who has never joined a group have broken the rules?\n\nI could even add one more point: the Creator Guidelines state that a world can't \"Preemptively moderate users by using a static or dynamic \"block list\" or similar systems\".. but being able to ban a user, even who isn't present in a group (a community group and a group for a world), be a kind of block list that prevents access to certain instances? Like public group instances?..\n\nThank you.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
