      "value": "unfortunately, I want to mention you all agreed to the Terms of service stating that if you don't follow rules, you would be punished and unfortunately most groups besides mine don't even enforce the terms of service which you are supposed to otherwise vrchat wouldn't have let you play vrchat it's not a do I have to its yes you have to, so to get upset over something like allowing groups to have public instances where they can and will enforce their own rules is a valid argument seeing how vrchat has already told you agree to the terms of service or don't play vrchat. I am not going to agree on something that shows how people won't follow the terms of service even after they signed off on it.",
