      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "> \"there are some worlds where administrators abuse the system by instructing users to create public group instances under the pretext of \"protection\", when in reality, this is done solely to prevent banned users from participating. This misuse of the system undermines the integrity of public group instances.\"\n\n@{63cbea337d46b409827e402a|full_name}: As someone who is also impacted by a similar scenario, a world author having beef with me and posting signs in their world to use their official group for instances, I agree that it can be annoying. But in my case the world author has shown to be pretty toxic on their own so their group is barely used, and people like to use their own groups instead now so they have moderation powers over the instances they make, so this barely affects me now.\n\nI have had more issue with the world author abusing their *world author moderation powers* to kick me from any public instances on sight. This includes them joining me in my own Group Public instance and kicking me out of it, which has forced me to have the world creator banned from my group. See: [remove-world-creator-moderation-powers](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/remove-world-creator-moderation-powers)\n\nSorry for ranting a little bit.\n\nBasically put. This is the intended use of Group Public instances and groups. If you want to not be in a Group Public instance, just don't be. Does that mean sitting in a new Public instance alone until likeminded people join you, yes maybe. But it wouldn't be much different then them causing drama over you being in *their* instance and forcing you out by other means. Learning to leave and make a new instance instead of staying in a toxic instance is an important skill for any VRChat player.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
